<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      Voice + push capable release manifest (Android Repair 07).

      BOTH CAPABILITIES. This is the fourth and last state of the governed
      matrix in android/app/build.gradle:

        push OFF / voice OFF -> src/release        (neither grant)
        push OFF / voice ON  -> src/certification  (RECORD_AUDIO only)
        push ON  / voice OFF -> src/push           (POST_NOTIFICATIONS only)
        push ON  / voice ON  -> src/voicePush      (this file, both)

      It exists because an Android build-type source set has exactly ONE
      manifest slot, so two independent capabilities that can each be on or
      off need a file per combination. Its content is deliberately nothing
      more than src/certification's Voice block plus src/push's push grant,
      over the same src/release base -- there is no policy here that is not
      already stated in one of those two files, and
      scripts/check-native-config-parity.js holds all four to the same base
      so they cannot drift apart.

      This is the combination staging-certification builds today
      (EXPO_PUBLIC_SMART_WATCHLIST_V1=true plus KSCAN_VOICE_CERTIFICATION=true
      in eas.json). That is a fact about today's certification profile, not a
      coupling: either capability can be activated without the other, and the
      three sibling manifests above are what prove it.

      WHAT THIS FILE MUST NEVER CONTAIN: a <service> element, a
      foreground-service microphone permission, a background-capture
      permission, or any re-grant of the foreground-service permissions
      Repair 02 removed.
    -->

    <!-- Carried verbatim from src/release/AndroidManifest.xml. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW" tools:node="remove"/>

    <!--
      Voice grant -- identical to src/certification/AndroidManifest.xml. See
      that file for the full Voice rationale; it is the governed home of this
      policy and this line is its combination-variant restatement.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO" tools:node="replace"/>

    <!-- Push grant -- identical to src/push/AndroidManifest.xml. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" tools:node="replace"/>

    <!--
      Capture permissions, explicitly denied even here. Voice Scan is strictly
      foreground and strictly just-in-time; there is no capture path that could
      need either. MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS is deliberately NOT listed: Repair 03
      established that it is a PLAYBACK-ROUTING permission expo-audio
      contributes for Elise speech, not a capture permission, and removing it
      here would strip audio routing from an artifact that still plays Elise.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MICROPHONE" tools:node="remove"/>
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAPTURE_AUDIO_OUTPUT" tools:node="remove"/>

    <!-- Repair 02 foreground-service removals, restated for this variant. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE" tools:node="remove"/>
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK" tools:node="remove"/>

</manifest>
